> isqrt4(x: u4) = isqrt(x)
> gates isqrt4
gates for isqrt4: 4 input bits -> 4 output bits (2 constant), basis c
  minimal: cost 5, 5 steps (no program of cost <= 4 exists; 660213 candidates searched)
  checked: the program reproduces every output bit on all 16 care inputs
  t0 = or(x0, x1)                = x0 | x1
  t1 = or(x2, x3)                = x2 | x3
  t2 = or(x2, t0)                = x2 | t0
  t3 = xor(x3, t1)               = x3 xor t1
  t4 = xor(t2, t3)               = t2 xor t3
  r3 = 0
  r2 = 0
  r1 = t1
  r0 = t4
> gates isqrt4 max 3
gates for isqrt4: 4 input bits -> 4 output bits (2 constant), basis c
  exact search stopped (cost limit at cost 3); Shannon decomposition instead:
  cost 5, 5 steps (an upper bound, not proved minimal)
  checked: the program reproduces every output bit on all 16 care inputs
  t0 = or(x0, x1)                = x0 | x1
  t1 = xor(x3, t0)               = x3 xor t0
  t2 = and(x2, t1)               = x2 & t1
  t3 = xor(t0, t2)               = t0 xor t2
  t4 = or(x2, x3)                = x2 | x3
  r3 = 0
  r2 = 0
  r1 = t4
  r0 = t3
